Third-party software notices
============================

eiviz itself is MIT-licensed. Native SDKs are optional, feature-gated, and
never vendored into the default build. Operators must obtain their own
licenses before enabling the corresponding Cargo features.

NDI
---
NDI is a trademark of Vizrt NDI AB. The NDI SDK is proprietary. Default
builds compile `eiviz-io-ndi` without linking the SDK and report the
capability as unavailable. Enabling `ndi-sdk` requires a valid NDI SDK
license from Vizrt and compliance with the NDI SDK license agreement.

OMT (Open Media Transport)
--------------------------
The OMT adapter uses MikanseiLaboratory/openmediatransport-rs and vmx-rs,
pure-Rust independent community implementations licensed under MIT. It does
not link or fall back to libomt.

Blackmagic DeckLink / Desktop Video
-----------------------------------
The Blackmagic Desktop Video SDK is proprietary. Default builds compile
`eiviz-io-decklink` as a capability stub. Linking the official SDK requires
accepting Blackmagic Design's SDK license.

ASIO
----
ASIO is a trademark and technology of Steinberg Media Technologies GmbH.
An ASIO adapter is not linked in default builds. Shipping ASIO support
requires a Steinberg ASIO license or an alternative GPLv3-compatible path
that is kept out of the MIT binary.

H.264 / AVC
-----------
The software encoder in `eiviz-codec-software` emits Baseline I_PCM access
units for tests and an explicitly selected software recording profile. Product distributions that encode
or decode AVC in the field may require MPEG-LA / Via LA patent licenses.
The planned software decode profile dynamically loads an end-user-installed
Cisco OpenH264 2.6.0 binary. It must not be bundled and must display
"OpenH264 Video Codec provided by Cisco Systems, Inc." with Cisco's binary
license. Compiling OpenH264 source does not receive Cisco's binary patent
coverage and is not the selected profile.
AAC encoding is not included in the default tree; PCM or a separately
licensed encoder must be used until an AAC adapter is certified.

gpu-video
---------
The optional `eiviz-codec-gpu-video` crate may depend on gpu-video 0.4.x
(MIT) behind a feature flag. It is not compiled into the default GUI path
so wgpu 24 (egui) and wgpu 29 (gpu-video) cannot collide.

GStreamer / FFmpeg
------------------
Neither GStreamer nor FFmpeg is a default dependency. If a distribution
enables those adapters, their LGPL/GPL obligations apply to that build
only and must be documented in the shipping SBOM.
